## Anatomy of a CSS Rule

A CSS rule has two parts:

```css
selector {
  property: value;
  property: value;
}
```

- **Selector** — identifies which HTML elements to style.
- **Declaration block** — wrapped in `{}`, contains one or more declarations.
- **Declaration** — a `property: value` pair ending with a semicolon.

## Example

```css
/* Rule targeting all <p> elements */
p {
  color: #333;          /* text color */
  font-size: 1rem;      /* font size */
  line-height: 1.6;     /* spacing between lines */
}
```

## At-Rules

Beyond standard rules, CSS has **at-rules** that control how rules are applied:

```css
/* @media — applies rules at specific viewport sizes */
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  p { font-size: 0.875rem; }
}

/* @keyframes — defines animation steps */
@keyframes fadeIn {
  from { opacity: 0; }
  to   { opacity: 1; }
}

/* @layer — controls cascade layer order */
@layer utilities {
  .sr-only { position: absolute; width: 1px; }
}
```

## Multiple Selectors

Comma-separated selectors apply the same declarations to multiple targets:

```css
h1, h2, h3 {
  font-weight: 700;
  color: #111;
}
```

## The CSS Box Model

Every HTML element generates a rectangular box with four layers:

```
┌─────────────────────────────┐  ← margin (transparent, pushes others away)
│  ┌───────────────────────┐  │  ← border
│  │  ┌─────────────────┐  │  │  ← padding (background color shows here)
│  │  │    content      │  │  │
│  │  └─────────────────┘  │  │
│  └───────────────────────┘  │
└─────────────────────────────┘
```

## content-box vs border-box

```css
/* Default (content-box) */
.box {
  width: 200px;   /* content only */
  padding: 20px;  /* adds 40px → total rendered width: 240px */
  border: 2px solid; /* adds 4px → total rendered width: 244px */
}

/* border-box — recommended */
*, *::before, *::after {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}
.box {
  width: 200px;   /* includes padding + border → stays 200px */
  padding: 20px;
  border: 2px solid;
}
```

## Margin Collapsing

Vertical margins between block elements collapse to the larger of the two values:

```css
.first  { margin-bottom: 24px; }
.second { margin-top: 16px; }
/* Gap between them = 24px, not 40px */
```

Collapsing does **not** happen with Flexbox or Grid children, or when a parent has `overflow: hidden`.
